{"appendix":true,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:489442d83a6b22a72c997fafaae70b88eef59185db5d81af1c829351af45271a","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026#cor:three-cell","title":"Three-cell smoothing"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/683ede37e1d945edf211dd64.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Corollary","generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"r:Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026:cor:three-cell","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026","name":"Three-cell smoothing","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"A.4","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/source/sections/matching-smoothing.tex","label":"cor:three-cell","line":324,"manuscript":"Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026","statement_sha256":"f6f915f527dc0f4761254b45c17a61b9f67dccbf79ec3d9d7fdb4d15738e3315"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026.html#cor:three-cell","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":7,"section_title":"Uniform smoothing of matching averages","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:4b7804fbfb5440dea0e43da31642ec1719a7bedb3e79b88ca7ce3e18ebe5981f","file":"preprints/Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026/build/source/sections/matching-smoothing.tex","line":324,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f6f915f527dc0f4761254b45c17a61b9f67dccbf79ec3d9d7fdb4d15738e3315","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026/build/source/sections/matching-smoothing.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4b7804fbfb5440dea0e43da31642ec1719a7bedb3e79b88ca7ce3e18ebe5981f","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Exponential-PSD-rank-of-positively-shifted-matching-matrices-October-5-2026/build/source/sections/matching-smoothing.tex#L324"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:three-cell}\nFor every fixed $K>0$, there are an integer $d\\ge1$ and $N_0$ with the following property. Let $N\\ge N_0$ be even, and let $a,b,c$ be positive integers summing to $N$. For a uniform ordered partition into cells of these sizes, prescribe $x,y,z$ edges between the first and second, first and third, and second and third cells, respectively. Assume that $x,y,z$ are nonnegative integers and that\n\\[\n a-x-y,\\qquad b-x-z,\\qquad c-y-z\n\\]\nare nonnegative even integers. Let $T_{x,y,z}$ average functions on perfect matchings subject to these counts, and let $\\Pi_d$ project onto the edge-product span of degree at most $d$, using uniform measures as above. Then\n\\[\n \\normop{T_{x,y,z}(I-\\Pi_d)}\\le N^{-K}\n\\]\nuniformly in all the sizes and admissible triples. For every fixed partition and matching function $f$, the values $T_{x,y,z}\\Pi_df$ are given by one polynomial of total degree at most $d$ in $(x,y,z)$ across all admissible triples."}
